# End-to-End QA Automation Platform

[![PR Smoke Tests](https://github.com/vaibhavkumar2001/End-To-End-QA-Automation-Project/actions/workflows/pr-smoke.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/vaibhavkumar2001/End-To-End-QA-Automation-Project/actions/workflows/pr-smoke.yml)
[![Nightly Regression](https://github.com/vaibhavkumar2001/End-To-End-QA-Automation-Project/actions/workflows/nightly-regression.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/vaibhavkumar2001/End-To-End-QA-Automation-Project/actions/workflows/nightly-regression.yml)

A test automation framework covering UI, BDD, API, accessibility and visual
regression, with CI/CD, sharded nightly runs, Allure reporting and Docker.

**Targets:** [SauceDemo](https://www.saucedemo.com) (UI) and
[Restful-Booker](https://restful-booker.herokuapp.com) (API)

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Dev[Developer] -->|pull request| PR[PR Smoke: tsc + @smoke tests]
    Cron[Nightly 02:00 IST] --> Nightly[Nightly Regression]
    Nightly --> S1[Shard 1]
    Nightly --> S2[Shard 2]
    Nightly --> S3[Shard 3]
    Nightly --> S4[Shard 4]
    S1 --> Merge[Merge reports]
    S2 --> Merge
    S3 --> Merge
    S4 --> Merge
    Merge --> Reports[Playwright HTML + Allure]
    Merge --> Slack[Slack notification]
```

## What is covered

| Layer | Tooling | Location |
|-------|---------|----------|
| UI | Playwright, Page Object Model, custom fixtures | `pages/`, `fixtures/`, `tests/ui/` |
| BDD | Gherkin via playwright-bdd | `features/`, `steps/` |
| API | Typed client, Zod schema validation, negative cases | `api/`, `tests/api/` |
| Accessibility | axe-core (WCAG 2 A/AA) | `tests/ui/a11y.spec.ts` |
| Visual regression | Playwright snapshots (Linux baselines) | `tests/ui/visual.spec.ts` |
| Test data | Faker factories, per-test data creation | `utils/` |

## Design decisions

- **BasePage:** shared navigation and assertion helpers, so page objects stay small.
- **Fixtures:** page objects and the API client are injected, so tests never build them by hand.
- **Schema validation:** API tests check response shape and types, not only status codes.
- **Independent tests:** every test creates its own data, so tests run in parallel safely.
- **Known API quirks are tested, not hidden:** for example, Restful-Booker returns 201 on delete and 200 on bad credentials.

## Tech stack

Playwright, TypeScript, playwright-bdd, Zod, Faker, axe-core, Allure,
GitHub Actions, Docker

## Getting started

```bash
npm ci
npx playwright install --with-deps chromium
cp .env.example .env
```

## Running tests

```bash
npx bddgen                                   # generate specs from .feature files
npx playwright test                          # everything
npx playwright test --project=ui             # native UI specs
npx playwright test --project=bdd            # BDD scenarios
npx playwright test --project=api            # API tests
npx playwright test --grep "@smoke"          # smoke subset
```

### Run in Docker

```bash
docker compose build
docker compose run --rm tests
```

Visual regression baselines are Linux-only. Generate or update them in Docker:

```bash
docker compose run --rm tests sh -c "npx playwright test tests/ui/visual.spec.ts --project=ui --update-snapshots"
```

## CI/CD

| Pipeline | Trigger | What runs |
|----------|---------|-----------|
| PR Smoke | Every pull request | Type check, then `@smoke` tests (quarantined tests skipped) |
| Nightly Regression | 02:00 IST and manual | Full suite in 4 parallel shards, merged Playwright and Allure reports, Slack notification |

## Results

| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Automated tests | 20 (8 UI, 4 BDD, 8 API) |
| PR smoke duration | about 1 min (see the Actions tab) |
| Full nightly duration with 4 shards | about 1.5 min (see the Actions tab) |

## Flaky test policy

1. **Detect:** CI retries failed tests twice. Tests that pass on retry are marked
   "Flaky" in the Playwright report and reviewed after each nightly run.
2. **Reproduce:** `npx playwright test <file> --project=ui --repeat-each=10`
3. **Quarantine:** tag the test with `@quarantine`. Quarantined tests are skipped
   on pull requests but still run nightly, so they stay visible.
4. **Fix the root cause:** log it in the table below, fix it, then remove the tag.
5. **Prevent:** no hard waits; use auto-waiting `expect(locator)` assertions;
   every test creates its own data.

| Test | Root cause | Fix |
|------|-----------|-----|
| (none yet) | | |

## Project structure

```
api/          typed API client and Zod schemas
features/     Gherkin feature files
fixtures/     custom Playwright fixtures (UI and API)
pages/        page objects (BasePage + pages)
steps/        BDD step definitions
tests/ui/     UI, accessibility and visual specs
tests/api/    API specs
utils/        test data factories
.github/      CI workflows
```

## Roadmap

k6 load test for the API, and LLM-assisted generation of Gherkin scenarios.